    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Reduced Row Echelon Form of a Singular 3x3 System With One Pivot",
    "problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-x-y-3z=1 \\\\ 2x+2y+6z=-2 \\\\ -2x-2y-6z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
    "worked_solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -2 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
