    "reasoning": "All 16 final answers agree with the captured worked solutions. The source_error judgment concerns an intermediate transcription error in q-73958: the displayed corresponding system says x-2y-6z=8, but its echelon matrix correctly represents x+2y-6z=8. Its conclusion of no solution remains correct. For q-12558 and q-14434, integration by parts gives e^{ax+b}(kx/a-k/a^2)+C. For q-14451 and q-12565, integrating the sine factor first gives the stated cosine term and sine correction; differentiation verifies all four antiderivatives. In q-74536, both remaining rows are multiples of the first, leaving one nonzero row. In q-74604, elimination gives z=-6, y=13, x=40. In q-135370, A^2=I. In q-135391, A=I+N with N^2=0, so A^{-1}=I-N. In q-10662 and q-73958, elimination yields contradictions 0=-3 and 0=34, respectively. In q-4471, cancellation gives (x+sqrt(x))/x, whose limit is 2. In q-34153, 5a_1+a_2-3a_3=0 is a nontrivial dependence, so only II is true. In both plane questions, perpendicularity to the normal gives 2b-c=0; nonzero v ensures c is nonzero, so b/c=1/2. In q-73612, pivots occupy columns 1, 3, 5. In q-73638, row swaps produce pivots in columns 1, 2, 3, 4. No submission grades were supplied; each MA answer below is supported by its own captured worked solution.",
